course: dictionary
lesson: 11471
title: The word adviser
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: An adviser is a person whose job is to give advice, especially to help someone make a decision. Advice is the help itself, and the adviser is the one who gives it.
explain: «The Prime Minister asked her advisers for new ideas before the big decision.» Asked, ideas and decision are the clues. Someone is helping a leader choose, so adviser must mean a person who gives advice. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "people who give advice" still fits.
explain: Advisers work in many places. A careers adviser helps pupils choose their future jobs, and a financial adviser helps people look after their money. In old fairy tales, kings have wise advisers, or wicked ones who give bad advice.
fact: An adviser is a person whose job is to give advice.
fact: Advisers help people make decisions.
fact: «The king listened carefully to his wise advisers.»
fact: A financial adviser helps people with their savings and money.
fact: Advice is the help you are given; an adviser is the person who gives it.
exercise: «The Prime Minister asked her advisers for ideas.» Who are the advisers? | *People whose job is to give advice | People who sell ice cream | Animals that live on a farm | Pupils in a class
exercise: What does an adviser do? | *Gives advice to help someone decide | Cooks dinner for the family | Runs the fastest race | Paints pictures on the walls
exercise: A financial adviser helps people with | *their savings and money | their homework songs | their pet dogs | their football boots
test: «The wise adviser told the king to be kind to the farmers.» What did the adviser do? | Won a race | Built a new castle | Sold the king's horse | *Gave the king advice
test: What is the job of an adviser? | *Giving advice to help someone make decisions | Mending roads | Cutting hair | Driving buses
exam: «At school, Ravi went to see the teacher adviser before choosing his subjects.» Why did Ravi see the teacher adviser? | To buy a new school bag | *To get help making a choice | To tell a joke | To learn to swim
